Task: Move all four missions onto the framework (AC7) — Phase 5

Summary
-------
Fire, ice cream, park and puppy each hand-rolled the same lifecycle: a
`let state` variable, a transition assignment in every verb, a
`completeElapsed` timer and a `toIdle()` that cleared their own side data.
All four now declare their stages once and let `createMissionFsm` own the
transitions, the one-transition-per-event lock and the linger. AC7's grep
proof: `completeElapsed`, `let state`, `toIdle` and `state = '<literal>'`
now appear only inside `missionFsm.ts`; the four mission modules contain
zero bespoke transition code.

Framework gap closed (in-flight refinement, workflow.md
"Task Correction & Plan Amendment")
--------------------------------------------------------
`missionFsm` had `onCelebrate` and `onAbort` but no hook for the third
lifecycle edge — the linger landing back in idle — which is exactly where
fire's `fireHouseId`/`burstsLeft` and ice cream's `orderHouseId` are
dropped. Without it a mission would have to mask stale fields behind the
current state, which is the plumbing this module exists to delete. Added
`onIdle?: (from: S) => void`, red-first (5 new tests in
`missionFsm.test.ts`: emits once on the idle edge, never re-emits while
idle, once per completed run, silent on abort, plus the linger's
negative-frame clamp that moved out of four mission timers into the
framework).

Per-mission mapping
-------------------
- fire      -> `createMissionFsm` config (idle/spawned/driving/active/complete,
               linger 2.5 s); `onIdle`/`onAbort` -> `clearFire`
- iceCream  -> same stage set + linger; `onIdle`/`onAbort` -> `clearOrder`;
               `serve()` is now `attempt('active','complete')`
- park      -> idle/spawned/responding/collecting/complete; `finish()` is
               `attempt(['responding','collecting'],'complete')`; no side data,
               so no hooks
- puppy     -> idle/searching/carrying/complete; `siren()` is
               `attempt('idle','searching')`; `onIdle`/`onAbort` -> `clearPup`

